@page "/Bunion/About"
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About The Bunion";
    ViewData["Description"] = "About The Bunion — America's Finest Satirical News Source. Who we are, what we do, and why we should be stopped.";
}

<div class="bunion-about-page">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-8">

        <h1 class="bunion-headline bunion-headline-xl" style="border-bottom:3px solid var(--bunion-black); padding-bottom:16px; margin-bottom:24px;">
          About The Bunion
        </h1>

        <p class="bunion-lead">
          The Bunion is a satirical news publication dedicated to illuminating the absurdities of modern life through the noble art of making stuff up and presenting it as news.
        </p>

        <h2 class="bunion-headline bunion-headline-lg" style="margin-top:32px;">Who We Are</h2>
        <div class="bunion-article-body">
          <p>
            The Bunion was founded on the principle that the world is deeply, profoundly funny, and that the only appropriate response to the daily flood of bewildering events is to add more bewildering events — fictional ones — and see if anyone notices the difference.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our team of dedicated writers, editors, and headline crafters work tirelessly to produce content that sounds like it could be real, isn't, and might actually be more coherent than some real news in a pinch.
          </p>
          <p>
            We cover politics, science, health, business, sports, entertainment, and anything else that strikes us as sufficiently absurd — which, given the state of things, is basically everything.
          </p>

          <h2 class="bunion-headline bunion-headline-lg" style="margin-top:32px;" id="disclaimer">Legal Disclaimer</h2>
          <div style="background:#fff8dc; border:2px solid #e6c200; padding:20px 24px; margin:16px 0; border-radius:2px;">
            <p><strong>THE BUNION IS A SATIRICAL PUBLICATION.</strong></p>
            <p>All articles, headlines, names, quotes, and other content published on The Bunion are entirely fictional and are intended for entertainment and satirical purposes only.</p>
            <p>The Bunion does not claim that any of its articles represent real events, real people, real organizations, real studies, real legislation, or real journalistic practices. Any resemblance to actual events, living or dead persons, or actual organizations is purely coincidental and, frankly, impressively coincidental.</p>
            <p>Do not make decisions — financial, medical, legal, culinary, romantic, or otherwise — based on content you read on The Bunion. If you have done so, we would very much like to hear about it, because it sounds like a great story.</p>
            <p>The Bunion is not responsible for:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Embarrassment caused by sharing our articles as real news</li>
              <li>Confusion resulting from our articles being more plausible than actual current events</li>
              <li>Any existential crises triggered by the realization that satire and reality have become indistinguishable</li>
              <li>The lingering feeling that things were funnier before</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <h2 class="bunion-headline bunion-headline-lg" style="margin-top:32px;">Our Mission</h2>
          <p>
            To afflict the comfortable, comfort the afflicted, and make both groups feel vaguely embarrassed about something they read over breakfast.
          </p>
          <p>
            We believe that satire is one of democracy's most important tools — a way of puncturing pomposity, highlighting hypocrisy, and reminding powerful institutions that someone is paying attention and also writing jokes about them.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also just think a lot of things are very funny, and we want to share that with you.
          </p>

          <h2 class="bunion-headline bunion-headline-lg" style="margin-top:32px;">Our Standards</h2>
          <p>The Bunion is committed to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Being clearly, unambiguously satirical at all times</li>
            <li>Writing headlines that are funny, even when you already know it's fake</li>
            <li>Treating all subjects with equal irreverence</li>
            <li>Ensuring our fictional studies have better methodology than some real ones</li>
            <li>Using serif fonts, because that's what newspapers use and we are very serious</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top:40px; padding:20px; background:var(--bunion-black); color:white;">
          <h3 style="font-family:var(--bunion-serif); font-size:1.2rem; color:white; margin-bottom:8px;">The Bunion</h3>
          <p style="font-family:var(--bunion-sans); font-size:0.85rem; color:#aaa; margin:0; font-style:italic;">
            "America's Finest Satirical News Source" — a claim we make without evidence, in the finest tradition of journalism.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
